        "problem": "Differentiate ${e}^{x}tan\u2061x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=tan\u2061x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}tan\u2061x)^{\u2032} & ={u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{\u2032}\\cdot tan\u2061x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (tan\u2061x)^{\u2032} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(tan\u2061x)+({e}^{x})({sec}^{2}\u2061x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{sec}^{2}\u2061x+{e}^{x}tan\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
